# GDScript

Do not shadow engine methods. `PhysicsBody3D.test_move()` exists; a player field named `test_move` warns at reload.

```gdscript
❌ var test_move := Vector2.ZERO
✅ var forced_move_input := Vector2.ZERO
```

Headless tests drive movement through `forced_move_input` (`player.set("forced_move_input", Vector2(0, -1))`), not by faking OS key events.

Keep gameplay working without an LLM. Authoritative state stays in engine types and resources, not prose.
